ding (keeping its carried cause), :release, :cap, :policy,\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1457:     :silence. The :silence clauses are barred for leases on truncated\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1460:  5. reclaim each due lease by the injected procedure, marking it pending\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1463:  6. record :lapsed; on :dao.stream/ok the lease leaves the ledger.\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1467:  tick is observed. A drain ending in :dao.stream/end retires that cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1471:  before step 4: an aborted pass reclaims nothing, so a broken reader is\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1485:          (reclaim-and-record judge))))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1488:(defn restart\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1489:  \"A grantor that has lost its ledger reclaims and re-grants: for each\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1491:  optionally :max -- it performs the reclaim first, then grants afresh,\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1493:  seeds with its now. The reclaim ends the prior tenure; a new grant alone\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1496:  Returns `{:judge ... :unreclaimed [item...] :discarded-queue [fact...]}`.\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1497:  Items whose reclaim did not report success (or threw) are returned under\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1498:  `:unreclaimed` and are not re-granted -- a possessed resource that cannot\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1499:  be reclaimed is reported, not skipped silently. The stale queue of grants\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1510:        reclaim (:reclaim judge)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1511:        {:keys [reclaimed unreclaimed]}\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1513:                  (if (nil? reclaim)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1514:                    (throw (ex-info \"dao.lease: restart needs a reclaim procedure\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1517:                          (boolean (reclaim (get item :subject)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1520:                      (update acc :reclaimed conj item)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1521:                      (update acc :unreclaimed conj item))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1522:                {:reclaimed [] :unreclaimed []}\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1530:                                        (grant (mint-lease-id)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1536:                                                 {:dao.lease/max cap})))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1538:                      reclaimed)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1540:     :unreclaimed unreclaimed\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1551:;; (H3), release when done (H4). Nothing here installs a timer, renews on a\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1557:;; -- no ledger, no mutable state; a holder holding several leases threads\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1558:;; one state per lease. The bound bounds attention, not access (H5): every\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1562:(defn initial-holder\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1566:  :self              this holder's identity -- the :dao.lease/holder value\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1597:                     \"the holder needs its identity: the :dao.lease/holder it observes grants for\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1633:     :released? false\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1638:(defn renewal-interval\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1739:(defn observe-grant\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1742:  (`:dao.lease/holder` = `:self`) whose author, by the composition's\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1749:  grant naming another holder or another lease's proposal, a\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1766:  release it, but every discipline function treats it as at the bound --\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1770:  once, and no later fact moves it (a fresh lease id is a different\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1771:  lease; a holder holding several threads one state per lease). A\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1776:           (lease-fact? fact)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1777:           (= :dao.lease/accepted (get fact status-key))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1779:           (= (:self holder) (get fact :dao.lease/holder))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1783:               (= (:subject holder) (get fact :dao.lease/subject)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/le