e\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1896:  contract names): a second call returns `:release` nil and the holder\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1901:  (if (:released? holder)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1902:    {:holder holder :release nil}\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1904:                         \"a holder that has observed no grant holds nothing to release\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1906:        {:holder (assoc holder :released? true)\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1907:         :release (release (get-in holder [:grant :dao.lease/lease]))})))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1910:(defn holding?\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1912:  a grant has been observed (the right lease, when expectations were\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1922:                (not (:released? holder))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1934:;; that grants leases (C1-C4). Both validate the config's INJECTED SEAMS\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2060:  judge, nor the rule for which incarnation may reclaim, nor fencing --\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2114:(defn make-judge\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2115:  \"Assemble the judge half of a composition that grants leases (C1-C4).\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2117:  :drain-budget :resolver :reclaim :policy :writer :self :answer -- of\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2196:    (check-assembly! (fn? (get config :reclaim))\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2197:                     \"the judge needs a reclaim procedure per subject: (fn [subject] -> success?), idempotent, reporting\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2198:                     {:reclaim (get config :reclaim) :refused :reclaim})\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2215:(defn make-holder\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2216:  \"Assemble the holder half of a composition that grants leases (C1-C4).\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2228:                     renewals and releases for the judge to read. A\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2230:                     nothing: its lease would lapse in silence (C1's\nsrc/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:2239:  resolver, appends renewals and releases to `(:handle (:writer v))`,\nsrc/cljc/dao/leas